# inheritance

> "The hierarchy must be designed early, often as the first step of designing the program, and early decisions can be difficult to change once the program is written." - [Rob Pike][composition]

> "A decision to proceed with the hierarchy accepts that the risk that you may not yet have enough information to identify the correct abstraction."  - [Sandi Metz][poodr]

> "When your problem is one of needing numerous specializations of a stable, common abstraction, inheritance can be an extremely low-cost solution."  - [Sandi Metz][poodr]

